		{
			"id": "exMrY_6xoTahcTnBt",
			"description": "Autopistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cheap, mass-produced sidearm found across a billion hive worlds: gang muscle, PDF conscripts and Guard officers who don't rate a laspistol all carry one. Consistently portrayed in Guard and Arbites fiction as the low-status \"poor man's laspistol.\"\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers stub weapons, so this is built from scratch as a real-world-style light service pistol at TL7 (per framework.md's stub-tech tier), not lifted from any catalogue. 2d pi- averages 7, halved by the pi- wounding modifier to ~3.5 — a real but unimpressive threat to an unarmoured target, matching the autopistol's reputation as a backup weapon rather than a main-line arm. The Manstopper usage swaps to pi+ (bigger wound multiplier) with an armour divisor of (0.5), the standard GURPS way to model an expanding round: more damage to flesh, worse against any DR.",
