		{
			"id": "eMqUJlv_ICTqngWle",
			"description": "Autogun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard-issue solid-slug battle rifle of regiments and militias that lack a lasgun allocation — a recoil-operated intermediate-calibre rifle that recurs across Astra Militarum background material as the \"poor cousin\" of the lasgun, more common on low-priority garrison and PDF postings.\n\nDesign: Calibrated to lasgun parity rather than to flak. In the fiction autoguns kill as readily as lasguns, and Only War gives both the same damage (1d10+3), so the autogun sits at 4d+1 pi against the lasgun's 4d burn: avg 15, getting ~7 through flak (DR 8) and rarely beating carapace (DR 20), the same outcomes as the lasgun. An earlier draft used 2d+2 pi to make flak \"stop stub rounds\"; that framework wording was about pistol calibres and has been corrected. Range 500/2000 fits an intermediate-calibre rifle. RoF 10, 30(3) follow selective-fire rifle conventions. The Dum-Dum usage applies the same expanding-round logic as the autopistol's Manstopper.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "150",
			"base_weight": "8 lb",
