		{
			"id": "eGE58NvXGebFKBY9S",
			"description": "Stub Revolver",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A well-made, reliable break-top or swing-cylinder handgun favoured by Inquisitorial acolytes, enforcers and anyone who prizes reliability over firepower or rate of fire; FFG-line background (used here only for relative calibration, per framework.md's source order) singles the stub revolver out as the higher-quality, slower-firing counterpart to the stub automatic.\n\nDesign: Single-action cycling caps RoF at 1 — there's no autofire mechanism. Full pi wounding (rather than the autopistol's pi-) and a higher base die (2d+1) reflect a larger-calibre, better-machined round fired from a tighter, hand-fitted barrel; low Rcl (1) follows from GURPS convention for a heavier, well-balanced revolver.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
