		{
			"id": "euoNQNsracKvxragr",
			"description": "Stub Automatic",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The cheaper, select-fire cousin of the autopistol and stub revolver, common as a backup piece among gangers, cultists and low-tier militia; distinguished in FFG-line background primarily by cost and magazine capacity rather than raw power.\n\nDesign: Same round as the autopistol's standard ball ammunition (2d pi-), since both fire generic mass-produced pistol-calibre cartridges — the difference is a smaller magazine (10+1 vs. 16+1) and cheaper construction, reflected here in cost and weight rather than a duplicate damage figure, since GCS has no separate build-quality stat.",
