			"id": "egbMrzIvOXBAZnZmZ",
			"description": "Heavy Stubber",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's standard heavy machine gun: a deliberately archaic solid-slug design valued precisely because a forge world with almost no infrastructure can still manufacture it. A mainstay on Chimera pintles, Sentinel weapon mounts and heavy-weapon squads across Guard background art and fiction, and never once shown killing a tank.\n\nDesign: Scaled up from the autogun's pi rating to a true heavy-calibre weapon (pi+, the GURPS x1.5 wounding multiplier), reasoned from a real-world heavy support-gun analogue rather than any catalogue entry. Deliberately pitched below the heavy bolter anchor (8d(2) pi+, which \"chews light vehicles\"): 5d+1 pi+ averages ~19 with no armour divisor, nowhere near AV10's DR 50. That failure is intentional — the fiction never shows a heavy stubber meaningfully hurting a vehicle, only infantry, and this stat block reproduces that gap explicitly. Mounted per framework.md's braced/mounted-heavies rule, hence Gunner (Machine Gun) rather than Guns.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "900",
			"base_weight": "40 lb",
			"weapons": [
