		{
			"id": "elmowmV1PexTMlHay",
			"description": "Combat Shotgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A full-auto-capable military scattergun issued to void-ship boarding parties, PDF close-quarters units and Adeptus Arbites riot squads. \"Executioner\" shells are referenced in FFG-line background (relative calibration only, per framework.md) as a specialist close-range, armour-beating round issued to elite units rather than line troops.\n\nDesign: Buckshot and slug follow the usual GURPS shotgun split — short-ranged and hard-hitting versus long-ranged and precise — but are given single flat damage figures rather than the Basic Set's full range-banded pellet-spread rules, a deliberate simplification noted here for transparency. The Executioner shell keeps the buckshot's short range but adds an armour divisor of (2), modelling a penetrator flechette payload that trades general usefulness for beating armour at point- blank range.",
